  "prompt": "Support `cp_file`/`mv` for buckets in `HfFileSystem` (breaks write-then-rename libraries like `torch.distributed.checkpoint` and `datasets`)\n\nI've been testing with buckets as \"S3 for training outputs\" and hit: `HfFileSystem.cp_file` raises `NotImplementedError(\"Copy from/to buckets is not available yet\")` for bucket paths, and fsspec's `mv`/`rename` go through it. So anything that writes a temp file and then renames it fails on `hf://buckets/\u2026`. \n\nTwo examples:\n\n- `torch.distributed.checkpoint` with `FsspecWriter(\"hf://buckets/<user>/<bucket>/ckpt\")` writes all the shards, then fails renaming `.metadata.tmp`, so you end up with a checkpoint that has no `.metadata`. (Mounting the bucket on Jobs works fine; this is for people writing straight to `hf://` from their own machines.)\n- `datasets`: `download_and_prepare(\"hf://buckets/\u2026\", file_format=\"parquet\")` (the [S3 route in the docs](https://huggingface.co/docs/datasets/package_reference/builder_classes#datasets.DatasetBuilder.download_and_prepare)) and `load_dataset(..., cache_dir=\"hf://buckets/\u2026\")` fail the same way and leave temp shards behind.\n\nIt seems like copy was planned (#3807: \"iso-feature (except copy-file for now)\"). I know there's bigger work happening on HfFileSystem and buckets (edit/append in #4752, Xet range reads in #5045), but IIUC this path isn't directly related, and it should be simpler, since it only relies on existing primitives. #4752 already has a same-bucket `cp_file` that does a server-side copy by xet hash via `_batch_bucket_files`, which works on 2.0 today. I tried that bit on its own locally: about 0.4 s per copy regardless of file size, and `fs.mv` plus the DCP save above both work. Is it worth splitting out so it can ship before the edit/append work? It's not super urgent but could be quite low effort to add? \n\ncc @lhoestq",
